From b6dcf97faf59c22c7b35fab91a17d956eb354a94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karel Kadlec <xkk@post.cz>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:34:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] m17-bridge: add a web dashboard for messages and an SMS send
 form

The dashboard shows every message the bridge handled - RF to APRS-IS,
APRS-IS to RF and messages sent from the dashboard - with the source
callsign of the station rather than the gateway callsign, and offers a
form that transmits an M17 SMS to the radios connected to the bridge
module.

- web: new package with the message store (in-memory ring plus a JSONL
  history that survives a restart), the HTTP API and a self-contained
  dashboard page (no new dependencies, Go stdlib only).
- server: the APRS module hands each message it sends or receives to a
  Recorder, logs it at INFO level (message traffic was invisible at the
  configured INFO log level because it was logged at DEBUG), reports its
  link state and registered users, and no longer fails to start when
  APRS-IS is unreachable - the read loop keeps retrying.
- inet: expose the connected clients, and do not panic in Close when the
  listen socket was never opened.
- cmd/m17-bridge: [Web] configuration, SMS sending that bypasses the APRS
  module on purpose (a message from the dashboard is a transmission, not
  an APRS message), and a non-zero exit when the inet server stops.
